<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.3.2: Exploring Different Growth Patterns</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01276</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.3.2: Exploring Different Growth Patterns</md:title>
    <md:uuid>05b7a2e4-9a0b-4dbd-be8b-009f8af32fcb</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity </title>
      <para id="para-00001">You are walking along a beach, and your toe hits something hard. You reach down, grab onto a handle, and pull out a lamp! It is sandy. You start to brush it off with your towel. Poof! A genie appears.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">He tells you, “Thank you for freeing me from that bottle! I was getting claustrophobic. You can choose one of these purses as a reward.”</para>
      <list id="list-00001">
        <item> Purse A, which contains $1,000 today. If you leave it alone, it will contain $1,200 tomorrow (by magic). The next day, it will be $1,400. This pattern of an additional $200 per day will continue.</item>
        <item> Purse B, which contains 1 penny today. Leave that penny in there because tomorrow it will (magically) turn into 2 pennies. The next day, there will be 4 pennies. The amount in the purse will continue to double each day.</item>
      </list>
      <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00002">
        <exercise id="_9564b84f-59c5-4f7e-b457-b98e34c19378" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            <para id="para-00003"> How much money will be in Purse A after a 7-day week? <emphasis>Enter your answer as a number rounded to the nearest cent.</emphasis></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Correct! After 7 days, Purse A will contain $2,400 because it grows by $200 each day for 7 days.</para>
            <para id="para-00005">Nice try! The correct answer is 2400. After 7 days, Purse A will contain $2,400 because it grows by $200 each day for 7 days.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="fed6efed-4317-45ce-a13b-a080b7ff4dba" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            <para id="para-00006"> How much money will be in Purse B after a 7-day week? <emphasis>Enter your answer as a number rounded to the nearest cent.</emphasis> </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Correct! Purse B will contain $1.28. It doubles each day for 7 days, so it will have \(1 \cdot 2^7\) or 128 cents (the 1 here represents the 1 cent for when the genie appeared).</para>
            <para id="para-00008">Nice try! The correct answer is 1.28. Purse B will contain $1.28. It doubles each day for 7 days, so it will have \(1 \cdot 2^7\) or 128 cents (the 1 here represents the 1 cent for when the genie appeared).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="b629a372-a46b-450c-ac6f-d7937f0a8131" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            <para id="para-00009"> How much money will be in Purse A after two weeks?<emphasis>Enter your answer as a number rounded to the nearest cent.</emphasis></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00010">Correct! After 2 weeks, Purse A will contain an additional $1,400 for a total of $3,800.</para>
            <para id="para-00011">Nice try! The correct answer is 3800. After 2 weeks, Purse A will contain an additional $1,400 for a total of $3,800.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4d0fd695-2745-4efd-a5ef-7e257f13d678" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            <para id="para-00012"> How much money will be in Purse B after two weeks?<emphasis>Enter your answer as a number rounded to the nearest cent.</emphasis></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00013">Correct! Purse B will contain \(1 \cdot 2^{14}\) cents. This is 16,384 cents or $163.84.</para>
            <para id="para-00014">Nice try! The correct answer is 163.84. Purse B will contain \(1 \cdot 2^{14}\) cents. This is 16,384 cents or $163.84.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_08d4eb51-8e61-4e80-b05a-60c31ec88bfd" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            <para id="para-00015"> The genie later adds that he will let the money in each purse grow for three weeks. 
          
          <para id="para-00016">How much money will be in Purse A in three weeks?<emphasis>Enter your answer as a number rounded to the nearest cent.</emphasis></para>
         </para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00017">Correct! After 3 weeks, Purse A will have an additional $1,400 during the third week for a total of $5,200.</para>
            <para id="para-00018">Nice try! The correct answer is 5200. After 3 weeks, Purse A will have an additional $1,400 during the third week for a total of $5,200.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_6b4c4909-37b7-4c7e-b283-c10dcc995503" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            <para id="para-00019">How much money will be in Purse B in three weeks? <emphasis>Enter your answer as a number rounded to the nearest cent.</emphasis></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00020">Correct! Purse B will have 128 times as much money (compared to the end of two weeks) for a total of $20,971.52.</para>
            <para id="para-00021">Nice try! The correct answer is 20971.52. Purse B will have 128 times as much money (compared to the end of two weeks) for a total of $20,971.52.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c4c68a98-fd64-4611-9fd6-e3c1eff0eb8b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            <para id="para-00022"> Which purse contains more money after 30 days? <emphasis>Enter your answer as a number rounded to the nearest cent.</emphasis></para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00023">Correct! Purse B will have a lot more money. Purse A will have \(1,000+30 \cdot 200\) or $7,000, which is much less than the doubling purse has on day 21.</para>
            <para id="para-00024">Incorrect. Purse B will have a lot more money. Purse A will have \(1,000+30 \cdot 200\) or $7,000, which is much less than the doubling purse has on day 21.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <note id="note-00001">
        <para id="para-00025">Building Character: Grit</para>
        <div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-gap-1">
          <figure id="fig-00001">
            <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
              <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_05_03_01.png"/>
            </media>
          </figure>
          <div>
            <para id="para-00026">Grit is passion and perseverance to reach long-term goals.</para>
            <para id="para-00027">Think about your current sense of grit. Are the following statements are true for you?</para>
            <list id="list-00002">
              <item>
          Setbacks don’t discourage me for long.
       </item>
              <item>
          I never stop working to improve.
       </item>
            </list>
            <para id="para-00028">Don’t worry if none of these statements are true for you. Developing this trait takes time. Your first step starts today!</para>
          </div>
        </div>
      </note>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>